---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const b = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const faqs = [
  ['How much does Booke AI cost compared with Digits?', 'Booke AI Business is $129 per business per month; the firm plan is custom-priced. Digits is priced per client: Essentials $65 per month and Core $100 per month, with Pro $250 listed as coming soon, and no per-seat fees.'],
  ['Does Digits replace QuickBooks Online or Xero?', 'Yes. Digits is its own AI-native general ledger, so clients move off QBO or Xero. Booke AI works inside the existing QBO or Xero file instead.'],
  ['Which is cheaper for 20 clients?', 'At list price, Digits Essentials is 20 × $65 = $1,300 and Core is $2,000 per month, with the ledger included. Booke AI Business is 20 × $129 = $2,580 per month, plus the QBO or Xero subscriptions.'],
  ['Can firms with non-US clients use Digits?', 'Digits supports US entities only. Booke AI fits clients outside the US because it runs on their existing QBO or Xero books.'],
];
const faqLd = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a } })),
});
---
<Base
  title="Booke AI vs Digits for bookkeeping firms — AI on top of QBO/Xero vs an AI-native ledger"
  description="Booke AI ($129/business/mo, daily AI categorization inside QuickBooks Online and Xero) vs Digits ($65-$100/client/mo, AI-native general ledger that replaces QBO/Xero, no seat fees): who keeps the ledger, what each automates, and 20-client cost math. Prices verified Oct 2026."
>
  <h1>Booke AI vs Digits</h1>
  <p>Both put AI on the daily bookkeeping work, but they make a different bet about the ledger. Booke AI works inside the client's existing QuickBooks Online or Xero file: it categorizes the bank feed every day, matches documents, and flags exceptions for your staff. Digits replaces QBO or Xero with its own AI-native general ledger that categorizes and reconciles continuously, priced per client with no seat fees. The real question is whether you want to move clients off their current ledger.</p>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th></th><th><a href={`${b}/tools/booke-ai`}>Booke AI</a></th><th><a href={`${b}/tools/digits`}>Digits</a></th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Firms that want to keep every client on QBO or Xero and cut the daily coding work</td><td>Firms willing to move clients to a new ledger in exchange for one AI-native platform across all clients</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pricing (verified Oct 2026)</td><td>AI Bookkeeper (Business): $129 per business/month, prorated when you add a business mid-period. Firm plan (multi-client management, white-label, priority onboarding) is custom-priced.</td><td>Per client: Essentials $65/mo, Core $100/mo; Pro $250/mo is listed as coming soon. No per-seat fees; firm's own books free on Free Firm Books; 30-day free trial.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Ledger</td><td>Your existing QuickBooks Online or Xero file. You still pay for that subscription.</td><td>Digits is the ledger (replaces QBO/Xero). US entities only.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>What it automates</td><td>Daily bank feed categorization, smart document matching, missing document requests, rules and thresholds, OCR for bills, invoices and receipts, exception review with audit trail</td><td>Continuous AI categorization and reconciliation in the ledger, reporting and dashboards; firm plans add practice management and close tools</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Switching cost</td><td>Low: connect to the file the client already has</td><td>High: migrate each client's books and get the client used to a new system</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Cost at 20 clients (list prices, monthly)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Booke AI Business: 20 × $129 = $2,580, plus the QBO or Xero subscriptions you or your clients already pay. The firm plan is custom-priced, so a firm at this size would likely ask for a quote.</li>
    <li>Digits Essentials: 20 × $65 = $1,300. Core: 20 × $100 = $2,000. The ledger is included, so the QBO or Xero subscription goes away.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>At list price Digits is cheaper per client and also removes the ledger fee, but that saving only shows up after you migrate each client. All figures before discounts or promotions; neither firm-level discount is published.</p>

  <h2>When to choose Booke AI</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your clients are staying on QBO or Xero, or some are outside the US.</li>
    <li>You want AI on the coding work without a migration project.</li>
    <li>You want OCR and document matching for bills, invoices and receipts, or a white-labeled client experience (firm plan).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to choose Digits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your clients are US entities and you are open to moving them to a new ledger.</li>
    <li>You want a published per-client price with unlimited team seats.</li>
    <li>You are onboarding new clients and can start them on Digits instead of QBO or Xero.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  {faqs.map(([q, a]) => (<><h3>{q}</h3><p>{a}</p></>))}
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqLd} />

  <p>Sources: booke.ai/pricing and digits.com/pricing, checked 2026-10-19. No sponsor has paid for this comparison.</p>

  <p>
    <a href={`${b}/compare/booke-ai-alternatives`}>Booke AI alternatives</a> ·
    <a href={`${b}/compare/digits-alternatives`}>Digits alternatives</a> ·
    <a href={`${b}/compare/digits-vs-xenett`}>Digits vs Xenett</a> ·
    <a href={`${b}/compare/booke-ai-vs-xenett`}>Booke AI vs Xenett</a> ·
    <a href={`${b}/compare/bank-reconciliation-tools`}>Bank reconciliation tools</a>
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f6f6f6; }
</style>
